# No operator PWA development in rinse-api

**Do not rebuild the legacy operator PWA UI** (jobs/clients/settings shells, PWA tour, service worker operator chrome) in `rinse-api/`.

## Forbidden without an explicit ask

- Operator UI pages, CSS, sheets, onboarding PWA, paywall operator chrome
- “Parity” ports of native screens back into Next operator routes
- Asking whether to implement operator features on PWA vs native

## Allowed in `rinse-api` (when product needs it)

- `/api/*` routes used by mobile or customers
- `/book/*`, `/portal/*`, `/embed/*`, `/admin/*`, legal pages
- Shared `@rinse/core` (`packages/core`) and PocketBase (`pocketbase`)

## Do instead

- **Operator product work → `rinse-mobile/` only**
- Shared types/schemas → `packages/core`
- Backend/customer web → `rinse-api` only for API / book / portal / admin

## If unsure

Stop and ask. Default for operator UI: **`rinse-mobile/` only.**
